<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.20.xsd">

  <!--
      RENAME FOLLOW-UP for 001 — repoint the seeded `fe-default` route from the
      host shell's half-renamed Service name (hugmesh-systems-web) to its final
      one (hugmesh-host-shell).

      BACKGROUND. The Angular host shell was renamed from its original
      pre-rebrand Service name to hugmesh-host-shell. An intermediate sweep left it
      as `hugmesh-systems-web`, a hybrid that carries no banned token and so was
      invisible to every grep-driven rename sweep. hugmesh-generator's compose
      lane had already moved to `hugmesh-host-shell`; its CLUSTER lane (the
      Deployment/Service pair in specs/cluster/manifests/frontend/ and the
      rendered route in specs/cluster/apps/20-gateway-fe.yaml) moves in the
      companion PR. This changeset is the DB-seed half of that same move.

      WHY A NEW CHANGESET INSTEAD OF EDITING 001 IN PLACE.
      001-gateway-routes.xml is shipped and may already have run in live
      databases, so it is immutable history:
        1. The uri lives INSIDE 001's <changeSet>, so rewriting it changes that
           changeSet's Liquibase MD5. Every DB that already ran 001 would then
           fail startup with ValidationFailedException on a checksum mismatch.
        2. Even ignoring checksums, an in-place edit would NOT fix an already
           migrated DB: 001 is recorded RAN and never re-executes, so the live
           row would keep pointing at the dead Service name forever. Only a NEW
           changeset can migrate an existing row.
      Follows the canonical pattern in hugmesh-federation-api's
      039-rebrand-character-forge-remote-entry.xml.

      DEPLOY ORDERING. The value here must match the host shell's actual k8s
      Service name, which the companion hugmesh-generator PR renames. The two are
      safe to land in EITHER order — this changeset is guarded (see SAFETY) and
      the generator rename does not touch a live cluster until ArgoCD syncs — but
      the SYNC must not happen while the route still points at the old name, or
      the Service the /** catch-all dials will not exist and the front page 502s.

      NOT THE ONLY ROUTE SOURCE. Per this repo's README "Known gaps", neither the
      production Helm chart nor the local compose stack loads this overlay today;
      both deploy the shared hugmesh-gateway image with their own
      generator-rendered application-routes.yml. This changeset (and the
      application-fe.yml default beside it) therefore keeps THIS repo's own
      artifact self-consistent and correct for anyone who does run it — it is not
      what repoints the currently-deployed mesh.

      SAFETY. The preCondition matches the row ONLY while it still carries the
      exact pre-rename uri, so the changeset is idempotent (re-runs MARK_RAN) and
      it never clobbers an operator override of the route's uri. The same
      predicate is repeated in the <where> clause so a concurrent override
      between the precondition check and the UPDATE is a no-op rather than a
      silent overwrite. A rollback restores the pre-rename uri.

      Keep in sync with the default route/URI in application-fe.yml
      (fe-default / DOWNSTREAM_URI).
  -->

  <changeSet id="002-1-route-fe-default-to-host-shell" author="hugmesh">
    <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
      <sqlCheck expectedResult="1">
        SELECT COUNT(*) FROM gateway_routes
         WHERE route_id = 'fe-default'
           AND uri = 'http://hugmesh-systems-web.hugmesh-frontend.svc.cluster.local:80'
      </sqlCheck>
    </preConditions>

    <update tableName="gateway_routes">
      <column name="uri" value="http://hugmesh-host-shell.hugmesh-frontend.svc.cluster.local:80"/>
      <where>
        route_id = 'fe-default'
        AND uri = 'http://hugmesh-systems-web.hugmesh-frontend.svc.cluster.local:80'
      </where>
    </update>

    <rollback>
      <update tableName="gateway_routes">
        <column name="uri" value="http://hugmesh-systems-web.hugmesh-frontend.svc.cluster.local:80"/>
        <where>
          route_id = 'fe-default'
          AND uri = 'http://hugmesh-host-shell.hugmesh-frontend.svc.cluster.local:80'
        </where>
      </update>
    </rollback>
  </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
